<!-- Reduced wrench-level cube of CubeWrench-v0 (see callosum/envs/wrench_cube/env.py).

Model layout (PLAN.md "Среда CubeWrench-v0", TECH MINIMUM 1):
  * `core`      -- the cube body: a free-floating 5.7 cm box (half-size 0.0285 m,
                   mass 0.2 kg, inertia derived by MuJoCo from the box geometry);
  * `layer`     -- the active layer: a thin plate parented to `core` on a hinge
                   about the local +z axis, limited to [0, pi/2] (the face-turn
                   range). Its collision is disabled: the layer only exists as the
                   body the rotator's wrench acts on, there is no contact anywhere
                   in this sandbox.

Both agents act through `mujoco.mjData.xfrc_applied` (holder -> `core`, rotator ->
`layer`); there are deliberately NO actuators and NO equality constraints, so the
policy output is a raw 6D wrench and the physics is the whole dynamic.

MODEL ASSUMPTION of the design's non-additivity: the rotator's torque on the layer reaches
the core only through the hinge's COMBINED damping/frictionloss (`hinge_damping +
hinge_frictionloss`). That is what makes the rotator alone drift the core (its predicted
drift is validated in `WrenchCubeConfig.__post_init__`, against the success tolerance) and
forces the holder's counter-wrench. This is the reduced model's abstraction, not a contact
model -- the layer's collision is disabled and there are no contacts anywhere.

The hinge damping/frictionloss/armature values and the hinge `range` here are DEFAULTS
only: `WrenchCubeEnv` overwrites the `model.dof_*` entries and `model.jnt_range` from
`WrenchCubeConfig` (the config is the single source of truth for timing and DOF
parameters, per the repo convention "tunables live in configs/"), and each `reset`
replaces the hinge frictionloss with the sampled `layer_frictionloss`. The geometry and
the two masses are XML-owned (MuJoCo's `mj_setConst` does not recompute a body's inertia
when `body_mass` changes, so they are not written at runtime). The gravity-free option is
the design's "cube floats" assumption.
-->
<mujoco model="cube_wrench">
  <compiler angle="radian"/>
  <option timestep="0.005" integrator="implicitfast" gravity="0 0 0"/>

  <worldbody>
    <body name="core" pos="0 0 0">
      <freejoint name="core_joint"/>
      <geom name="core_geom" type="box" size="0.0285 0.0285 0.0285" mass="0.2"/>

      <!-- Thin plate sitting on top of the core; hinge axis = its local +z. -->
      <body name="layer" pos="0 0 0.0305">
        <joint name="layer_hinge" type="hinge" axis="0 0 1" range="0 1.5708"
               limited="true" damping="0.0001" frictionloss="0.00001" armature="0"/>
        <geom name="layer_geom" type="box" size="0.0285 0.0285 0.002" mass="0.02"
              contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
      </body>
    </body>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
